"prose": [
{
"from": 191,
"to": 193,
"text": "No live leg: the chunk drives no real `claude` (inputs#I1), so the block holds no `live` or `round` entry and no liveness probe. The harness smoke boots the fake agent on the backing, and G2 and G4 are read over its home between `status` and `cleanup`."
},
{
"from": 195,
"to": 199,
"text": "The contended reading's producer is step 8's one-off driver. It waits on another builder's link, so no reader can re-run it, and it is absent from the fence for that reason: it is a one-off witness whose record goes to `evidence/`, as a mutation kill run's does (`.claude/rules/testing.md`, 2026-10-04). The fence holds its reader (`jq -e -s …`), which the wrap re-runs over the record. The driver's known-verdict control is implement's one-shot run of step 8, in `evidence/driver-control.md`."
},
{
"from": 201,
"to": 205,
"text": "One control mutates source and reverts, so it is a one-shot run at implement and not an entry: step 3's remove-the-guard pair for each keeper (`evidence/keeper-control.md`). On every re-run the two keeper entries hold the same property. `evidence/backing.md` and `evidence/smoke-on-backing.md` are records implement writes (steps 0, 5, 7 and 9), not artifacts an entry produces, so no entry carries `artifact`; on a re-run the entry `test -L target/e2e-home && findmnt …` holds the backing and the smoke entries hold G2 and G4 over it."
},
{
"from": 207,
"to": 207,
"text": "That entry reads the host: it is green only where the link is in force, which is this dev host."
},
{
"from": 209,
"to": 211,
"text": "Five builders share this host. A red whose shape is a stalled start is, from this chunk on, a finding about the backing and not a reason to re-run: its log is read first, with what the other build dirs wrote in its window (`.claude/rules/verification-harness.md`, 2026-09-29 and its 2026-10-06 extension)."
}
],
